## 🎯 Quick Start

### Option 1: Desktop (Fastest - 2 minutes)

```bash
# Clone repository
git clone https://github.com/your-username/medbot-enhanced.git
cd medbot-enhanced

# Create virtual environment
python -m venv venv
source venv/bin/activate  # On Windows: venv\Scripts\activate

# Install dependencies
pip install -r requirements.txt

# Download NLTK data
python -c "import nltk; nltk.download('punkt'); nltk.download('wordnet')"

# Train the model (first time only)
python ml/training/train.py

# Run GUI
python gui.py
```

### Option 2: Web Application (2-3 minutes)

```bash
# Clone repository
git clone https://github.com/your-username/medbot-enhanced.git
cd medbot-enhanced

# Using Docker Compose
docker-compose up -d

# Application will be available at:
# Frontend: http://localhost:3000
# Backend API: http://localhost:5000
# Admin Dashboard: http://localhost:3000/admin
```

### Option 3: Docker Container (1 minute)

```bash
# Build Docker image
docker build -t medbot:latest .

# Run container
docker run -p 5000:5000 -p 3000:3000 medbot:latest
```

---

## 📦 Installation

### Prerequisites

- **Python**: 3.8 or higher
- **Node.js**: 14 or higher (for web frontend)
- **Docker**: 20.10+ (optional, for containerized deployment)
- **PostgreSQL**: 12+ (for production database)
- **Redis**: 6+ (for session management)

### Step 1: Clone Repository

```bash
git clone https://github.com/your-username/medbot-enhanced.git
cd medbot-enhanced
```

### Step 2: Backend Setup

```bash
# Create virtual environment
python -m venv venv

# Activate virtual environment
# Linux/Mac
source venv/bin/activate

# Windows
venv\Scripts\activate

# Install dependencies
pip install -r requirements.txt

# Download required NLTK data
python -c "
import nltk
nltk.download('punkt')
nltk.download('wordnet')
nltk.download('averaged_perceptron_tagger')
"
```

### Step 3: Model Training

```bash
# Train the NLP model (first time only)
python ml/training/train.py

# Expected output:
# Training Done
# Model saved as chatbotmodel.h5
# Vocabularies saved as words.pkl, classes.pkl
```

### Step 4: Database Setup (Optional)

```bash
# Initialize PostgreSQL database
psql -U postgres -f database/schemas/init.sql

# Set database URL in .env
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://username:password@localhost:5432/medbot
```

### Step 5: Run Application

```bash
# Option A: Desktop GUI (Tkinter)
python gui.py

# Option B: Flask API Server
python -m flask run --port=5000

# Option C: Full Docker Stack
docker-compose up -d
```

